            <ArticleTitle>Fatal air embolism during cardiopulmonary bypass: analysis of an incident and prevention measures.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>875-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/icvts/ivu242</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Air embolism is a life-threatening complication during cardiopulmonary bypass. We present a case of a patient who suffered an air embolism during coronary bypass surgery, despite standard safety features and procedures. The patient died 3 days after surgery due to massive cerebral oedema. This case report gives a reconstruction of the event and the countermeasures undertaken to minimize the risk of recurrence.</AbstractText>
